  "query_preview": "..\n(Tuesday night through Friday)\nIssued at 205 AM CDT Sat Oct 24 2026\n\nIf we do see this secondary wave Monday Night/Tuesday, it is\nprojected to move east of the area late Tuesday pushing the\nprecipitation chances northeast of the area.\n\nThere is now more consistent signal between the operational GFS\nand ECMWF of a large-scale trough developing across the western\nUnited States late this week, and ensemble cluster analysis only \nshows roughly a 13 percent chance of upper-level ridging from \nsouthwest Texas to the Intermountain West that yesterday's 00Z\noperational ECMWF run showed. So it is much more likely that we\nwill be in a pattern with southwesterly flow aloft. Precipitation\nchances increase late this week with the arrival of low-level\nmoisture from the Gulf and any shortwaves in the southwesterly\nflow aloft, however the timing of the best chances of showers and\nstorms will be a little uncertain as it will depend on timing of \nindividual shortwaves which are difficult to resolve this far in \nadvance.\n\nAfternoon highs will remain above average for this time of year as\nautumn-like air remains locked in the northwestern United States\nand western Canada through the week.",
